code(to:)","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CaCertificate\/encode(to:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"encode","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7EncoderP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"title":"encode(to:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/SE":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Encodable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SE"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CaCertificate/keyCustody":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"keyCustody","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cacertificate\/keycustody","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Which custodian holds this CA’s signing key. Recorded per CA rather than read from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"configuration, so adopting a new custodian does not strand the CAs that already exist."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Not secret — an operator needs to see it, and it discloses only where a key is kept."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"keyCustody","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CaCertificate\/keyCustody"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CaCertificate/subject":{"type":"topic","title":"subject","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The CA’s common name, e.g. ","type":"text"},{"code":"ACME Corp Root CA","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The normalised value: a ","type":"text"},{"code":"CN=","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" prefix in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the request is understood and stripped, so this always says what the certificate’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subject DN says (DF-023).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cacertificate\/subject","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CaCertificate\/subject","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"subject","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CaCertificate/tenantID":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"tenantID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The tenant this CA signs for, when it is a tenant signing CA. ","type":"text"},{"code":"None","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"organization-level CA — the trust anchor, and the only kind that existed before tenant"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"signing CAs. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Some"},{"type":"text","text":" for an intermediate created under one, which exists so a tenant’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"user, service and device certificates chain through a CA that can be revoked and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"replaced without touching the anchor the rest of the estate trusts.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cacertificate\/tenantid","role":"symbol","title":"tenantID","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CaCertificate\/tenantID"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CaCertificate/mtlsTrustAnchor":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cacertificate\/mtlstrustanchor","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CaCertificate\/mtlsTrustAnchor","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether this CA is offered as a trust anchor for mutual TLS. When set, the server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exports this CA’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"public"}]},{"type":"text","text":" certificate to the bundle named by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AXIAM__SERVER__TLS__CLIENT_CA_BUNDLE_PATH"},{"type":"text","text":" at startup and turns client-certificate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authentication on ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optional"},{"type":"text","text":") if the operator has not configured it explicitly. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"client presenting a certificate that chains to this CA is then verified by the TLS layer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"itself, which is what "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axiam_pki::mtls"},{"type":"text","text":" needs to authenticate an IoT device or a service"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account by certificate rather than by secret. # What is and is not copied Only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"public_cert_pem"},{"type":"text","text":" — the certificate. The "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"private key stays where its custodian put","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (Vault, or sealed into the row) and is never written to the server volume. A trust"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anchor is public by construction: it is what the server hands every client during the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TLS handshake, and every device that has to validate the chain already holds a copy. #"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Why a restart rustls builds its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootCertStore"},{"type":"text","text":" once, when the listener is constructed,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and actix-web binds that config for the process’s life. Toggling this changes what the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"next"}]},{"type":"text","text":" boot trusts, and the API says so in its response rather than pretending the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change took effect. Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":", so a deployment that never touches this keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly the TLS posture it has today."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"mtlsTrustAnchor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mtlsTrustAnchor"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic"}}}